{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/922831-alpha-predators-changelings","id":922831,"title":"Alpha Predators: Changelings","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-28T14:00:54-07:00","id":922831,"title":"Alpha Predators: Changelings","content":"Challenge: create a Changeling at the heights of Fae power. Start with the basic character creation. You gain 45 Experiences to raise Wyrd to 10. You have 250 Experiences for everything else. You must create an actual character, not a one-dimensional white-room collection of numbers. Describe at least in brief how you might play this character, or her background, fill in some details. Go into as much detail as you like, but give us at least a little context.<br /> <br /> To give credit where credit is due, I'm borrowing Claire Redfields idea (and even some of the wording, altered) for this thread.<br /> <br /> So what kind of Fae can you come up with that would make theTrue Fae trumble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T14:41:02-07:00","id":922856,"title":"","content":"First, stop at Wyrd 9. If you go to 10, she <i>becomes</i> a True Fae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T15:03:00-07:00","id":922864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/922831-alpha-predators-changelings?p=922856#post922856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, stop at Wyrd 9. If you go to 10, she <i>becomes</i> a True Fae.</div> </div> </div> </div>In much the same sense as getting Mastery in one Arcanum and Adeptitude in three more turns your Gnosis 6+ mage character into an archmaster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T15:22:40-07:00","id":922876,"title":"","content":"If my memory serves me correctly, once a changeling hits Wyrd 10 she starts periodically losing a dot of Clarity until she hits zero Clarity and becomes a True Fae. So not quite the same as the Archmastery thing, as it's something that happens involuntarily rather than being a choice the changeling makes; but it's similar in that it's not an instantaneous, automatic transformation, nor is it inevitable. Just very nearly so: most changelings aren't going to be able to counter the Clarity loss indefinitely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T15:29:42-07:00","id":922883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/922831-alpha-predators-changelings?p=922876#post922876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If my memory serves me correctly, once a changeling hits Wyrd 10 she starts periodically losing a dot of Clarity until she hits zero Clarity and becomes a True Fae.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your memory serves you incorrectly. &quot;This potentially happens at some narratively-determined point while you have Wyrd 10&quot; is not the same thing as &quot;This always begins to happen immediately once you hit Wyrd 10.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T16:14:24-07:00","id":922902,"title":"","content":"I personally thought that becoming a True Fae, if you use that in your game, would be scarier if it was something the character chose. But I digress. Let's assume that this does not happen for the purposes of this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T16:39:59-07:00","id":922909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/922831-alpha-predators-changelings?p=922856#post922856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, stop at Wyrd 9. If you go to 10, she <i>becomes</i> a True Fae.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>People, stop saying this. This is <b>wrong.</b></i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T16:45:12-07:00","id":922914,"title":"","content":"*WORK IN PROGRESS*<br /> <br /> Sar'sheen God(dess) of Sin and Darkness, Dark Lord of Hearts, the Lady of Noble Depravity aka Jeremy St. Avalon.<br /> <br /> Name: Sar'sheen Seeming: Darkling Kiths: Hunterheart/Dearheart Freehold: 1001 Nights Toronto Court: Ivory<br /> <br /> Stats: \u2022\u2022Int, \u2022\u2022Wits, \u2022\u2022\u2022 Res, \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Str, \u2022\u2022 Dex, \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Sta, \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Pre, \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Man, \u2022\u2022 Com<br /> <br /> Skills \u2022\u2022\u2022 Occult, \u2022\u2022\u2022 Crafts, \u2022 Academics, \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Brawl, \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Atheletics, \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Stealth \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Intimidate, \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Larceny, \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Subefuge, \u2022\u2022\u2022 Persausian, \u2022\u2022 Empathy, \u2022\u2022 Socialize, \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Animal Ken <br /> <br /> Contracts: \u2022\u2022\u2022 Control Elements (Darkness, D, E), \u2022\u2022 Spiders Boon (D, B), \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Air and Darkness (D, O, E), \u2022 Inanimate Commune (Viewing, D), \u2022\u2022\u2022 Discreet Conjuration (D, W), Phantom Glory \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 (Darkness, F, E), Paralysing Shudder \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 (D), \u2022\u2022\u2022 Mirror Walk (D, B), \u2022\u2022\u2022 Skinmask (B, F), \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Vainglory (D, F, W), Armour of the Elements \u2022\u2022\u2022 (Darkness, E, F), Pathfinder \u2022 (B, E), \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Chrystalsis (58xp on contracts), \u2022\u2022\u2022 Pipes of the Beastcaller (Big Cats, Small Cats)<br /> <br /> Merits: \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Goblin Vows (Mortal Vice, Polished Ivory, Absolute Darkness, Feverant Prayers, Ligers), \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Potent Kith, \u2022\u2022\u2022 Dual Kith, \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Hollow ( Temple Palace of Kkol'taashra, \u2022 Luxury, \u2022\u2022 Size, \u2022 Route Zero, \u2022 Shadow Garden), \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Court Goodwill Brass \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Court Good Will: Silver, \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022Court Goodwill Ash (of the London Courts), \u2022\u2022 Lethal Mien, (Burning Touch), \u2022\u2022\u2022 Hedge Beast Companion (Tiger), \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Mantle (Ivory Court, Toronto Freehold), \u2022\u2022 Hob Kin, \u2022\u2022\u2022 Exotic Airs (Ghosts, Vampires, the Unchained), \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Fae Mount (\u2022Many Leagues, \u2022\u2022 Dreamspun, \u2022\u2022Actorsmask), \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 MI: Cult of Mithra, \u2022 Library (Occult), \u2022 Allies (Cult of Mithra), Diviner \u2022\u2022\u2022 , \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Retainer, Resources \u2022\u2022\u2022, Alternet IDs Alexander P. Joneson, Alternate ID Crystal McMasters, Alternate ID Priya Gandhi (59xp merits)<br /> <br /> Backstory: Sar'sheen doesn't remember much of his mortal life, just his mortal name, how loyal he'd been to his parents, who'd sold him to a True Fae in exhange for a cure for his Sister's cancer.<br /> <br /> In Arcadia Jerameny, was renamed Sar'sheen, Pride Leader of a Gravedark Pride, a Pride of Night Ligeresses (Hunterhearts) owned The Princess of Enduring Screams.<br /> <br /> To transform Jeramy into Sar'sheen The Princess ripped out the still beating hearts of the entire Gravedark Pride, combined them with Jaremy's heart, and placed in back into his chest, turning him into a (Hunterheart/Dearheart) Night Liger Pride Leader.<br /> <br /> Sar'sheen betrayed his Pride simply by leaving Arcadia with their unified heart, without which the rest of the Pride entered a deathless sleep.<br /> <br /> Sar'sheen justifies the betrayal by reminding himself of all the horrors they inflicted on fellow Changelings and other Fae.<br /> <br /> Still Sar'sheen sees himself stained by the act of betrayal, so when Sar'sheen joined the Ivory Court he took on the role of God of Sin and Darkness.<br /> <br /> Sar'sheen's Mien is a mix of the Liger, Demonic, and Ivory Court influences.<br /> <br /> Sar'sheen has large horns of pure ivory, with tips of gold, his skin is red, but his eyes are feline, and his hair is that colour of Liger furr. Sar'sheen has a arrow tip shaped tail, a forked tongue, and disturbing sigil on his forhead.<br /> <br /> Across his body is a symbol representing each contract he knows. <br /> <br /> His Mantle is represented by his Ivory Horns and the piles of wealth that falls from his body in piles around him, yet which disappear when they leave his presence.<br /> <br /> Sar'sheen has what he calls his 3 Avatars, Priya, Alexander, and Crystal, all of whom were identies belonging to his former High Priests who died him his service.<br /> <br /> Unable to cope with their deaths, Sar'sheen permantently assumed their Identities, using Skinmask contract.<br /> <br /> His current High Priestess is Natalie Stonager, a beautuful, disgraced former RCMP officer, turned escort who swore her soul to Sar'sheen in exchange for eventual Gnosis with Sar'sheen like Priya, Crystal, and Alexander achieved.<br /> <br /> Sinwind is a Black Chariot pulled by six nude<br /> damned souls (Fae Mount). The Souls and the Chariot are a single entity and represent the mortal forms of the six Ligeresses of the Gravedark Pride that Sar'sheen betrayed, straight from one of Sar'sheen's nightmares.<br /> <br /> Lastly is Sar'sheen's wife, Velvet Claws, his Liger Hedge Beast Companion, with \u2022\u2022\u2022 Skinmask, \u2022 Armour of Elements (Darkness).<br /> <br /> Velvet Claws is a former Beast's horror broken free upon the Beasts death, Velvet Claws escaping to the Hedge becoming a Hedge Beast Companion. Velvet Claws prefers using Skinmask and Harden Mask to assume the stolen forms of mortal human women when outside of the Hedge or Combat, including her former mortal identity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 06-28-2016, 08:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T16:48:26-07:00","id":922915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/922831-alpha-predators-changelings?p=922856#post922856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, stop at Wyrd 9. If you go to 10, she <i>becomes</i> a True Fae.</div> </div> </div> </div> It was optional, and it was risking clarity lose everyday, so a daily breaking point which in Changeling 2e is alot swingier then 1e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T17:02:08-07:00","id":922922,"title":"","content":"I wanted someone more Gender Fluid, and it occurred to me that one could not only change Genders/Sex/Perhaps even Sexual orientation with Skinmask + Fairest Effect + Harden Mask, but that it would be cool, if extreme way an Immortal Changeling could keep dead mortal loved ones alive,within themselves in a sort of mystical Gnosis.<br /> <br /> I took a mixture of previous concepts, some new ideas, and the above to create Sar'sheen, God(dess) of Sin and Darkness (dispite the dark overtones Sar'sheen isn't evil, more mischievious, and debauchery masking deep seated pain).<br /> <br /> Sar'sheen isn't finished yet, 250xp is alot to spend, so He's a work in progress. Like I'm thinking that when Sar'sheen killed his fetch, it so terrified his Sister she ran into traffic and got hit by a Mac Truck.<br /> <br /> So as she dies Sar\u2019sheen promises to bring her back the only Sar'sheen knows how, by becoming his Sister at least part of the time, and that's how the idea of Gnosis with Sar'sheen started, an inablity to let go when a loved one dies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T18:23:08-07:00","id":925610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/922831-alpha-predators-changelings?p=922876#post922876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If my memory serves me correctly, once a changeling hits Wyrd 10 she starts periodically losing a dot of Clarity until she hits zero Clarity and becomes a True Fae. So not quite the same as the Archmastery thing, as it's something that happens involuntarily rather than being a choice the changeling makes; but it's similar in that it's not an instantaneous, automatic transformation, nor is it inevitable. Just very nearly so: most changelings aren't going to be able to counter the Clarity loss indefinitely.</div> </div> </div> </div> You've mixed up two optional setting/rules hacks here.<br /> <br /> The first one is that if changelings hit wyrd 10 and if they (as in both the player and the character) chooses to do so, they can undergo the transformation into a true fae. But getting to Wyrd 10 is a choice, as is the transformation, so the player and their character has to make at least two choices to get there. <br /> <br /> The second one is a variant of the first- Except in this one, wyrd isn't something that changeling buy but risk accumulating like mage's paradox every time they use their powers, and if the changeling pushes themselves to wyrd 10 they automatically start the transformation into a true fae. <br /> <br /> But if one is in a game in which you actually pay experience for wyrd, then obviously the game isn't using the second option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T19:21:30-07:00","id":925634,"title":"","content":"You to reach clarity zero first, and you get a breaking point per day just for being at Wyrd 10 in those optional rules, its not an automatic loss of clarity.<br /> <br /> And the way breaking points work in Changeling 2e, your as likely to end up Clarity 10 then Clarity zero and running off to Arcadia to become a True Fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T19:49:23-07:00","id":925644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/922831-alpha-predators-changelings?p=925634#post925634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the way breaking points work in Changeling 2e, your as likely to end up Clarity 10</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. 2e Clarity has it that a successful breaking point roll gives you a Condition that needs a pretty major story beat to earn a bonus dot of Clarity, and the Condition goes away faster without reward at lower Clarity.<br /> <br /> <i>Failing</i> a breaking point roll gives you a Condition that hangs around longer at higher Wyrd and <i>penalizes subsequent breaking rolls</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T20:01:32-07:00","id":925647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/922831-alpha-predators-changelings?p=922876#post922876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If my memory serves me correctly, once a changeling hits Wyrd 10 she starts periodically losing a dot of Clarity until she hits zero Clarity and becomes a True Fae. So not quite the same as the Archmastery thing, as it's something that happens involuntarily rather than being a choice the changeling makes; but it's similar in that it's not an instantaneous, automatic transformation, nor is it inevitable. Just very nearly so: most changelings aren't going to be able to counter the Clarity loss indefinitely.</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually, I think they can, especially if they do things like making a smartly designed pledge for +3 to all rolls, which includes breaking point rolls, get the armoured clarity contract, use their Seeming Bonus to get as much Clarity as possible, and use the touchstone merit to its maxium benifit, there is not reason not to remain above zero clarity forever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}